      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>The Sm and the Lsm proteins, characterised by the Sm-domain, have RNA-related functions. The Sm heptamer ring associates with four (U1, U2, U4, U5) snRNPs, while Lsm2-8 heptamer is part of the U6 snRNP. Another Lsm heptameric complex, Lsm1-7, which differs from Lsm2-8 by one Lsm protein, functions in mRNA decapping, a crucial step in the mRNA degradation pathway [[cite:PUB00082657]].</p>",
